{{!
	@typedef object Indicator
	@prop string id core-owned DOM id, pre-escaped by core as `mw-indicator-<name>`,
		for example `mw-indicator-good-article`
	@prop string class core-owned class list; core always sets this to `mw-indicator`
	@prop string html the indicator's own markup, authored in wikitext or by an
		extension, so it is emitted unescaped with a triple-brace expression

	Indicator[] array-indicators the page status indicators, supplied unchanged by
		core in SkinMustache::getTemplateData(); an empty list is the normal case and
		still yields an empty container
}}
{{! Included by exactly one of two mutually exclusive callers: PageTitlebar.mustache
	when the language button is absent, BeforeContent.mustache when it is present. Both
	branches test the same has-buttons-in-content-top flag, so this partial renders
	exactly once per page and needs no guard of its own. }}
{{! DO NOT RENAME the wrapper class emitted below, nor the per-indicator mw-indicator
	class. Both belong to the platform DOM contract, not to this skin: core refills the
	wrapper in mediawiki.page.preview.js, mediawiki.page.ready fires the public
	wikipage.indicators hook from its children, and gadgets and extensions select on
	both names. The wrapper is emitted unconditionally for the same reason; an empty
	one is inert. The Notion appearance lives entirely in
	resources/skins.notion.styles/components/Indicators.less, which targets these very
	names because skin.json disables the core interface-indicators feature. }}
<div class="mw-indicators">
{{#array-indicators}}
<div id="{{id}}" class="{{class}}">{{{html}}}</div>
{{/array-indicators}}
</div>
